  "id": "Compound::DB01625 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Isopropamide appears to interact with Chrm3 through a shared participation in receptor activity pathways, as evidenced by its binding to Chrm1, which is involved in multiple receptor-related functions. The evidence suggests that Isopropamide may influence Chrm3 via a mechanism involving G-protein coupled receptors, as it is linked to both muscarinic and acetylcholine receptor activities. These pathways are central to the regulation of cellular responses to neurotransmitters, and the overlapping involvement of Chrm3 in these processes implies a potential role for Isopropamide in modulating receptor function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Isopropamide could affect Chrm3, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
